                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "variable-tube-voltage":</h3><p>Some tube microphones allow their <b>tube voltage</b>, aka &#8220;bias voltage&#8221; or &#8220;heater voltage&#8221; to be altered. Tubes can be over- or under-driven, resulting in an audible change is the microphone&#8217;s timbre. </p><p>Overdriving a tube (meaning, at high voltages) for extended periods can shorten the life of the tube.</p>
